Template: nex-installer/title
Type: text
Description: Nex Core setup

Template: nex-installer/failed
Type: error
Description: Setup did not finish
 ${detail}

Template: nex-installer/hostname
Type: string
Default: nexcore
Description: Host name or fully qualified domain name:
 This name identifies the host in Nex Controller and in the pool it creates.
 Use ASCII letters, digits and hyphens, for example nexcore or
 nexcore.example.test.

Template: nex-installer/keymap
Type: select
Choices: us, gb, de, fr, es
Default: us
Description: Keyboard layout:
 The layout is applied to this console immediately and installed on the host.

Template: nex-installer/keymap-error
Type: error
Description: Keyboard layout not applied
 ${detail}

Template: nex-installer/timezone-area
Type: select
Choices: ${choices}
Default: UTC
Description: Timezone area:
 Choose UTC unless this host must report local time.

Template: nex-installer/timezone
Type: select
Choices: ${choices}
Description: Timezone:

Template: nex-installer/password
Type: password
Description: Root password:
 No ordinary user account is created. Use root at the local console or over
 SSH after installation.

Template: nex-installer/password-again
Type: password
Description: Re-enter the root password to confirm:

Template: nex-installer/password-error
Type: error
Description: Root password rejected
 ${detail}

Template: nex-installer/management
Type: select
Choices: ${choices}
Description: Management adapter:
 This adapter becomes the port of bridge br0 on the installed host and is the
 only interface that owns the default route and DNS. Other adapters can be
 configured without a gateway.
 .
 Choose Offline to install without a management network. Adapters can still be
 configured, and networking can be set up locally after the host reboots.

Template: nex-installer/no-nic
Type: note
Description: No network adapter was detected
 Nex Core installs offline on this host. Configure networking locally after the
 host reboots, or attach an adapter and start setup again.

Template: nex-installer/other-adapters
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Configure more network adapters?
 ${detail}
 .
 Answer no to leave remaining adapters unconfigured and continue. Answer yes to set
 IPv4 on each remaining adapter; each one still offers Disabled.

Template: nex-installer/mode
Type: select
Choices: ${choices}
Description: IPv4 configuration for ${nic}:
 ${detail}

Template: nex-installer/vlan
Type: string
Default: 0
Description: VLAN ID for ${nic}:
 Enter 0 for an untagged adapter, or 1 to 4094 for a tagged one. One VLAN per
 adapter is supported; trunks and bonds are not part of this release.

Template: nex-installer/address
Type: string
Description: IPv4 address and prefix length for ${nic}:
 Use CIDR notation, for example 192.0.2.10/24.

Template: nex-installer/gateway
Type: string
Description: Default gateway for ${nic}:
 Must be an address inside the prefix entered above. Leave this empty to
 install without a default route.

Template: nex-installer/dns
Type: string
Description: DNS servers:
 Space-separated IPv4 addresses. Leave this empty to use the servers supplied
 by DHCP on the management adapter.

Template: nex-installer/disk
Type: multiselect
Choices: ${choices}
Description: Installation disks:
 Select one disk for a single install, or two or more for RAID1 copies of one
 system disk. More disks mean more copies, not more space; usable size is the
 smallest selected disk. Survives until only one selected disk remains.
 Everything on the selected disks is erased; other disks are left alone. Every
 selected disk must be within 10% of the smallest.

Template: nex-installer/disk-error
Type: error
Description: Installation disks not accepted
 ${detail}

Template: nex-installer/no-disk
Type: error
Description: No installation disk was found
 Only writable, nonremovable disks of at least 16 GiB (24 GiB for the image edition) are offered, and none was
 detected. Attach a supported disk and start setup again. Installation media and
 removable devices are never offered as targets.

Template: nex-installer/erase
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Erase ${disk} and install Nex Core?
 Review these settings. Answering yes starts partitioning and destroys every
 existing filesystem on every disk listed above.
 .
 Host name: ${hostname}
 Timezone: ${timezone}
 Keyboard layout: ${keymap}
 .
 Management adapter: ${management}
 Adapters: ${adapters}
 DNS servers: ${dns}
 .
 Installation disks: ${disk}
 Capacity: ${disksize}
 Serial: ${serial}
 Layout: ${layout}
 .
 Answer no to go back and change any of these settings.

Template: nex-installer/mode
Type: select
Choices: Erase and install, Repair image
Default: Erase and install
Description: A Nex Core data volume was found on ${found}
 Erase and install wipes the selected disks and installs a new system. Repair
 image rewrites only the system partitions and boot files of these disks and
 keeps the data volume: the host name, settings, virtual machines and
 payloads stay as they are.

Template: nex-installer/repair-confirm
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Repair the system image on ${disk}?
 The system image and boot partitions of every disk listed are rewritten. The
 Nex Core data volume is kept. Answer no to go back.
